<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banu Djellab</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1414–1854</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Djellab dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Banu Djellab were the ruling dynasty of Touggourt and the oases of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oued-righ">Oued Righ</a> in the north-eastern Algerian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a> from about 1414 to 1854. Traditionally said to be of Marinid descent, they ruled as sultans over a mixed oasis population, at times paying tribute to the Ottoman beys of Constantine. French forces occupied Touggourt in 1854 and ended their independence.</p></div>
